Subject: [PATCH] 3.32.0: every run writes query.cs beside its report, and from
 the reports directory `dotnet run --file query.cs -- <verb> .` answers as
 `kronikol query` does, byte for byte, with no tool installed and no network:
 where the engine comes from (the run's own Kronikol.dll on .NET 10, else
 lib/net10.0 in the NuGet cache, at exactly the version, and the cache a
 NuGet.config moved), what it needs (the .NET 10 SDK), why --file, a
 global.json pinning an older SDK, a consumer's Directory.Build.props and
 .targets, no query.cs where a C# project would compile it (bin, obj and a
 dot-folder such as .logs/kronikol are fine), and one Kronikol did not write
 or cannot read is left alone (Querying Reports; query.py kept for a machine
 without the SDK). WriteQueryScript, default on (Report Configuration).
 query.cs beside the report, not in Run.json and never under runs/ (Generated
 Reports). The OptionNotApplied warning for a reports folder inside a project
 (Diagnostics and Debugging). The no-tool line in Debug this run (CI Summary
 Integration). query.cs in the uploaded artifact on both CIs, and what it
 needs on another machine (CI Artifact Upload). A merge writes it too, and the
 combined-report recipe uploads it (Merging Parallel Reports).
 Kronikol.Query.QueryCommand, public, net10.0 only (API Reference). Home and
 the AI integration prompt name it beside kronikol query

